  "schema": "elder-souls/levels@1",
  "id": "levels",
  "owner": "W1-21 — the level-up screen (ui.menu.levelup)",
  "source": "corpus/20-progression/RI-PRG01-soul-cost-curve.json, transcribed whole",
  "provenance": "Souls-side currency and curve (seam S2); Morrowind-side breadth of the stat sheet is RI-PRG02, whose ten attributes are named below.",
  "amendment_note": "REPLACED by W1-21. The previous file carried soul_cost_formula 'round(0.02*L^3 + 3.06*L^2 + 105.6*L - 895)', a five-row table whose values (673, 689, 706, 723) are the DARK SOULS reference column of RI-PRG01's table rather than ours, and a six-name Souls-style attribute list that contradicts game/data/progression/attributes.json's ten. The formula evaluated NEGATIVE below level 9, so the level-up screen displayed a souls-to-next of 0 at level 6 and RI-UIX03 L3 ('a mismatch is a hard fail — the number is decorative') was unpassable by any build. The curve below is RI-PRG01's canonical formula and its own 139-row table, transcribed, not re-derived.",
  "soul_cost_formula": "cost(n) = round(0.015*n^3 + 2.00*n^2 + 55*n + 300)",
  "formula_note": "n is the level being PURCHASED (going from n-1 to n). Level 1 is free. Single curve, no piecewise band.",
  "min_level": 1,
  "max_level": 140,
